h96-kernel-switch (8.0.0~r13) resolute; urgency=medium

  * try of release that is already default or running (or that current
    Image embeds) makes new generation when staged Image or DTB differs
    from in-boot generation; refused as before when both are equal.
  * Boot guard and confirm tell trial boot from fallback by Image banner
    (build number and date) when generations of same release differ
    there, else by boot id and h96ks/cur as before.
  * list prints generations under each release with roles default,
    trial, trial-previous, rollback-target and running; status prints
    generation lines; in-use and prune take generation names KREL.gN.

 -- Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:00:00 +0000

h96-kernel-switch (8.0.0~r12) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New read-only command dtb: board DTB path, layout (plain, managed,
    link), resolved file and recorded trial phase; h96-undervolt uses it.
  * New command dtb-plain: managed DTB link back to plain file with same
    content (temporary name, read-back, rename).
  * try refuses while h96-undervolt trial is recorded, and DTB change
    while h96-undervolt change is active (--keep-dtb accepted).
  * rollback refuses when plain board DTB differs from DTB of target
    generation; rollback --keep-dtb accepts it.

 -- Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0000

h96-kernel-switch (8.0.0~r11) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Generation layout: Image, uInitrd and board DTB link through
    /boot/h96ks/cur; one rename switches all three, so power loss
    never leaves mixed set. First try converts plain-name links with
    content-identical steps (hard links, DTB copy).
  * Generations never change once in place; retry builds new one and
    drops unused earlier attempts of same release.
  * Confirm and rollback survive power loss: boot guard finishes them.
  * Refuses Image whose embedded release differs from requested one.
  * New read-only commands: default, in-use (used by kernel packages).
  * Preset file keeps guard and timer disabled under systemctl preset-all
    until first try enables them.

 -- Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

